From 74de59af0034426b0b5be1c8fd0050b654afdc7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:59:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! avalanche: vote over SHA256-identified eCash mempool
 batches

When all vote records are finalized or in flight, the regular/batch work classification is empty. Calling selectNode with an always-false predicate then sets needMoreNodes despite a healthy quorum, causing periodic getavaaddr to query every peer forever. Return before node selection when no work can be polled; preserve all capability filters, weighted selection and quorum rules. Unchanged abc_p2p_getavaaddr fails before157s and passes after43s.

Tier: eCash (fixup to avalanche: vote over SHA256-identified eCash mempool batches)
---
 src/avalanche/processor.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/avalanche/processor.cpp b/src/avalanche/processor.cpp
index b1be66a5d8..336effc93c 100644
--- a/src/avalanche/processor.cpp
+++ b/src/avalanche/processor.cpp
@@ -2072,6 +2072,12 @@ void Processor::runEventLoop() {
                 if (std::holds_alternative<const MempoolBatchVoteItem>(item)) batches = true;
                 else regular = true;
             }
+            // No peer is needed when no item can be polled. Passing an
+            // always-false capability predicate to selectNode would falsely
+            // report a peer shortage and keep requesting every peer's address.
+            if (!regular && !batches) {
+                return;
+            }
             nodeid = peerManager->selectNode([&](NodeId id) {
                 return regular || (batches && nodeSupportsMempoolBatch(id));
             });
